# ==============================================================================
# PLAIN-ENGLISH FILE AUTOMATOR - QUICK REFERENCE GUIDE
# Every line starting with '#' is ignored by the script and will never run.
# ==============================================================================
#
# 1. VARIABLES & GLOBAL SETTINGS (Put these at the top of the file)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   $MY_VAR = C:\Path\To\Folder       -> Create reusable shortcuts for paths
#   POWER = ON                        -> Set to ON to run, OFF to pause
#   WATCH = $DL, C:\Users\Example\Desktop -> Comma-separated folders to monitor
#
# 2. RULE STRUCTURE (Evaluated from top to bottom; stops at first match)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   [Rule Name]
#   WHEN <condition>
#   AND <another condition>           -> Optional: all AND lines must be true
#   THEN <action>
#   THEN <second action>              -> Optional: chain multiple actions
#   AND KEEP GOING                    -> Optional: let later rules also run
#
# 3. CONDITIONS (Use after 'WHEN' or 'AND', or join with 'OR')
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   always                            -> Matches every file
#   not <condition>                   -> Reverses any condition below
#
#   File Extensions & Names:
#   extension is mp4, mkv, mov        -> Matches any listed extension
#   extension is not tmp, log         -> Excludes listed extensions
#   name contains Caseoh              -> Matches substring anywhere in name
#   name does not contain draft       -> Excludes substring
#   name starts with IMG_             -> Matches beginning of filename
#   name ends with _final             -> Matches end of filename (before .ext)
#   name matches wildcard *2026*      -> Supports * (any text) and ? (1 char)
#   name matches regex ^clip_\d+      -> Full regular expression matching
#   folder is Desktop                 -> Matches parent folder (for multi-WATCH)
#
#   File Size & Age:
#   size is over 100 mb               -> Units: b, kb, mb, gb (also: under)
#   age is older than 7 days          -> Units: minutes, hours, days (also: newer than)
#
# 4. ACTIONS (Use after 'THEN')
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   move to $DL\Folder Name           -> Moves file (auto-renames _1 if duplicate)
#   copy to D:\Backups                -> Copies file to another folder
#   rename to NewName.{ext}           -> Renames file in place
#   delete file                       -> Permanently deletes the file
#   log Custom message: {filename}    -> Writes a note into sorter.log
#
# 5. DYNAMIC TOKENS (Use inside paths, 'rename to', or 'log')
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   {filename}  -> Full name with extension (e.g., video.mp4)
#   {name}      -> Name without extension    (e.g., video)
#   {ext}       -> Extension without dot     (e.g., mp4)
#   {year}      -> 4-digit year              (e.g., 2026)
#   {month}     -> 2-digit month             (e.g., 11)
#   {day}       -> 2-digit day               (e.g., 13)
#   {folder}    -> Name of the watched folder(e.g., Downloads)
# ==============================================================================
